1. DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION

1.1 In this Agreement, unless the context otherwise requires:

"Agreement" means this Employment Agreement including any schedules and amendments;
"Company" means Nexus Technologies Private Limited, a company incorporated under the Companies Act 2013, having its registered office at 14th Floor, Pinnacle Tower, Bandra-Kurla Complex, Mumbai 400051;
"Employee" means Alex Morgan, residing at the address on record with the Company;
"Commencement Date" means 1 March 2024;
"Confidential Information" has the meaning given in Clause 13;
"Intellectual Property Rights" has the meaning given in Clause 14;
"Notice Period" means the period specified in Clause 8.1.

1.2 References to statutes include amendments or re-enactments.
1.3 Headings are for convenience only and do not affect interpretation.

4. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES

4.1 The Employee shall:
(a) carry out the duties assigned by the Company diligently and to the best of their ability;
(b) follow all lawful instructions, policies, and procedures of the Company;
(c) devote their full working time and attention to the duties of the role;
(d) act in the best interests of the Company at all times.

4.2 The Company may from time to time reasonably change the Employee's duties, responsibilities, or reporting line.

4.3 The Employee may be required to travel within India or internationally as reasonably required for the performance of their duties.

5. REMUNERATION AND BENEFITS

5.1 Basic Salary: The Employee shall receive a gross annual Cost to Company (CTC) of ₹18,00,000 (Rupees Eighteen Lakhs), payable in equal monthly instalments of ₹1,50,000, subject to applicable tax deductions.

5.2 Performance Bonus: The Employee shall be eligible for an annual performance bonus of up to 15% of the basic annual salary, subject to the Employee meeting or exceeding performance targets as determined by the Company.

5.3 Benefits: The Employee shall be entitled to:
(a) Provident Fund contributions as per applicable law;
(b) Employee State Insurance (ESI) where applicable;
(c) Group medical insurance coverage of ₹5,00,000 per annum for the Employee and immediate family;
(d) Annual mobile reimbursement of ₹12,000.

5.4 Salary Review: The Company shall conduct an annual salary review. Salary increments are at the sole discretion of the Company and are not guaranteed.

5.5 All remuneration is subject to deductions required by law.

9. TERMINATION FOR CAUSE

9.1 The Company may terminate this Agreement immediately without notice or payment in lieu of notice in the event of:
(a) gross misconduct;
(b) serious breach of any term of this Agreement;
(c) conviction of a criminal offence;
(d) fraudulent or dishonest conduct;
(e) wilful damage to Company property;
(f) serious breach of confidentiality obligations.

9.2 Disciplinary proceedings shall be conducted in accordance with the Company's Disciplinary Policy.

9.3 Termination for cause is without prejudice to any other rights the Company may have under law or contract.

10. GARDEN LEAVE

10.1 During any notice period, the Company may require the Employee to remain away from the workplace ("Garden Leave").

10.2 During Garden Leave, the Employee shall:
(a) remain bound by all terms of this Agreement;
(b) not commence any alternative employment;
(c) remain available to assist with handover matters;
(d) not contact clients, customers, or suppliers of the Company except as directed.

11. RETURN OF PROPERTY

11.1 Upon termination of employment for any reason, the Employee shall promptly return to the Company:
(a) all equipment, including laptops, mobile devices, and peripherals;
(b) all access cards and security credentials;
(c) all documents, records, and data in any format;
(d) any other property belonging to the Company.

11.2 The Employee must not retain copies of Confidential Information upon termination.

11.3 Failure to return property may result in deductions from the Employee's final settlement.

13. CONFIDENTIALITY

13.1 The Employee acknowledges that in the course of employment, they will have access to Confidential Information.

13.2 "Confidential Information" includes, without limitation:
(a) technical data, software code, and system architecture;
(b) client lists, pricing, and commercial strategies;
(c) financial information and business plans;
(d) personnel information.

13.3 The Employee shall:
(a) keep all Confidential Information strictly confidential;
(b) not disclose Confidential Information to any third party without written consent;
(c) use Confidential Information solely for the purposes of performing their duties.

13.4 Post-employment: These confidentiality obligations shall survive termination and shall remain in force for a period of two (2) years following the date of termination.

13.5 The obligation does not apply to information that:
(a) is or becomes publicly available through no fault of the Employee;
(b) is required to be disclosed by law or court order.

16. DISPUTE RESOLUTION

16.1 In the event of any dispute arising from or in connection with this Agreement, the parties shall first attempt to resolve the matter through good-faith negotiation.

16.2 If not resolved within 30 days, the parties shall submit the dispute to mediation under the rules of the Mumbai Centre for International Arbitration (MCIA).

16.3 If mediation fails, the dispute shall be referred to binding arbitration:
(a) Seat: Mumbai, India;
(b) Language: English;
(c) Rules: MCIA Arbitration Rules;
(d) Arbitrators: Single arbitrator agreed by both parties.

16.4 Nothing in this clause prevents either party from seeking urgent injunctive relief.
